    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat. Fry the ginger until fragrant, then add the garlic and onion and cook until the onion softens.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the chicken and stir until the outside is no longer pink, about 5 minutes.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Pour in the fish sauce and stir so the chicken takes it in for a minute or two.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the water and bring to a boil. Skim off the gray foam that rises to the surface.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Lower the heat, cover and simmer until the chicken is tender.",
        "minutes": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the papaya and simmer until it is tender but still holds its shape.",
        "minutes": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Taste and adjust with fish sauce and pepper. Turn off the heat, stir in the leaves and let them wilt in the hot broth.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Serve hot with steamed rice and a small dish of fish sauce on the side.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Chayote (sayote) is the usual stand-in for green papaya and cooks in about the same time. Add the leaves only after the heat is off, or they turn dark and lose their flavor."
